 "text_original": "So let's run the Booz Allen request for real. The Reader pulls out every claim, including a line asking us not to use the old phone number. The Scout checks our vendor master and the public registries through Zetaris. The new address doesn't match anything we know, so the Examiner sends the Scout back to dig. It walks Booz Allen's corporate family, forty-one companies, and finds it. The address is real, but it belongs to a different Booz Allen company that has never billed us. Decision: hold. The number to call comes from SEC filings, and the one in the letter goes on the do-not-use list.",
